    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0285" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6–448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-04T17:00:00-04:00">June 4, 1948—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>842. Full text by urgent tel Ambs Jun 4 speech or statement<anchor n="90"
                        xml:id="d217-f1"/> would be appreciated since some news agencies playing
                    story as virtual US official demand to ChiGovt to suppress student movement on
                    pain no more aid. One version asserts Amb on instructions Dept presented formal
                    note ChiGovt demanding suppressions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d217-f1" n="90" xml:id="d217-f1-content">
                <p>For text transmitted in telegram of June 5, by the Ambassador in China, see
                    Department of State, <hi rendition="#italic">United States Relations With
                        China</hi> (Washington, Government Printing Office, 1949), p. 869.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
